  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFA- HEAL Autism Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ike Foundation for Autism (IFA) is a non-governmental organization committed to supporting persons living with autism to live productive and fulfilling life. In their previous project with Voice, they facilitated capacity building for parents &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; caregivers of persons with autism, on coping mechanism; trained service providers like therapists and doctors on new methodologies to improve their services to the rightsholders. Under the previous project, IFA Parents Forum- a rich resource and information sharing platform was formed and this forum remains beneficial to the rightsholders till date. Current project will upscale the gains of the previous project by reaching out to more communities in Abuja, to benefit from existing platforms.

The overall Goal ofthe current project is to improve the welfare of people living with autism by facilitating access to essential services in health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; education; build the skills of more autistic caregivers and sensitize the public on autisms. To achieve this goal, the following activities are designed:

1. Sensitization of the public on autism and challenges facing the autism community.
2. Capacity building to improve the skills/abilities of parents, caregivers, and service providers to provide care and essential services for people with autism.
3. To improve access to health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; education for persons with autism by providing advisory services to foster inclusion of autistic community.

The change that IFA wants to see in this project is - improved skills in supportingpeople with autism, enhanced access to health &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; education, and more awareness on issues affecting the community.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ike Foundation for Autism (IFA) is a non-profit, non-governmental organization established in 2008 with the vision to Eliminate Autism Stigma while providing Services. Their mission is to HEAL Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) in Africa and enable all persons livingwith ASD achieve their full potential and live productive lives. They would like to enable all persons living within the Autism Spectrum Disorders (ASD)to achieve their full potential and lead productive lives. Their vision is to eliminate Autism stigma in Africawhile providing expert services. Their core values are compassion, integrity, inclusiveness and acceptance. The strategic focus of IFA  is around Awareness, Assessment, Inclusive health services, Early childhood Intervention, Educational services &lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;)&gt; Capacity building for Care givers,Parents, Therapist, Service providers &lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;(&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;&lt;(&gt;&lt;&lt;)&gt;)&gt;)&gt; Rightsholder groups.

They are registered with the Corporate Affairs Commission of Nigeria and have affiliations with reputable organizations such as AutismSpeaks USA. IFA also partners with the Federal Ministry of Health; Universal Basic Education Commission; Federal Bureau of Statistics; Federal Capital Territory Administration; National Planning Commission; and AfriHUB ICT Solutions for Africa.

IFA is managed bythe Board, while the day to day operation is handled by a team of dedicated staff, headed by the Director.

IFA has been a partner of Voice project in Nigeria since 2017.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ike Foundation for Autism</narrative>
